==============================================================================================================================
A.  ARITHMETIC -- reproduce g06's two Local Group numbers independently before arguing about them
==============================================================================================================================
  reproduced  g_B (2MRS r>3 Mpc + UNGC r<3 Mpc, MW and its own satellites removed) = 6.0245e-15 m/s^2 = 0.000064 a_0        [g06 quotes 6.024e-15 / 0.00006]
  reproduced  g_L (2M++ linear reconstruction, mask 3 < R < 200 Mpc/h)             = 1.1608e-12 m/s^2 = 0.012401 a_0        [g06 quotes 1.161e-12 / 0.01240]
  reproduced  g_N from inverting g_L through nu(y) y a_0 = g                       = 1.4219e-14 m/s^2 = 0.000152 a_0     [g06 quotes 1.422e-14 / 0.00015]
  the inversion is the deep-MOND square root: g_N = g^2/a_0 gives 1.4395e-14, i.e. 1.24% from the numeric inversion, so E1's ratio is (g_B a_0)^(1/2)/g_L SQUARED and a factor r in g_N is only sqrt(r) in acceleration
  [PASS] A1 g06's three Local Group numbers reproduce from the same files with independent code.  If this failed the rest of the audit would be moot   (g_B 6.0245e-15 vs 6.024e-15 (+0.01%), g_L 1.1608e-12 vs 1.161e-12 (-0.02%), g_N,inv 1.4219e-14 vs 1.422e-14 (-0.01%))
  [PASS] A2 and E1's headline ratio reproduces, so the 'factor 0.42' is arithmetically what g06 says it is   (g_B/g_N,inv = 0.4237 against g06's 0.424; the raw factor is 193 against g06's 193)

==============================================================================================================================
B.  LIKE-FOR-LIKE -- E1's two sides do not contain the same volume, and one of them is M31
==============================================================================================================================
  g_B splits as  |far (2MRS, r > 3.0 Mpc)| = 1.0157e-14  and  |near (UNGC, r < 3.0 Mpc)| = 1.0143e-14
  they are 145 degrees apart, so they partly CANCEL: |far + near| = 6.0245e-15 is SMALLER than the far term alone.  E1's central number is a cancellation residual, not a sum.
    the near term, largest contributors      D/Mpc   g_N (m/s^2)  share of |near|
    MESSIER031                                0.78     8.918e-15             0.88
    SMC                                       0.16     5.442e-15             0.54
    MESSIER033                                0.86     9.093e-16             0.09
    MAFFEI2                                   2.80     5.118e-16             0.05
    DW1                                       2.80     2.519e-16             0.02
  g_L's mask starts at R > 3 Mpc/h = 4.45 Mpc, so the 2M++ side contains NOTHING inside 4.45 Mpc -- no M31, no Local Group at all.
  matched-volume baryonic field (2MRS only, r > 4.45 Mpc, no UNGC term at all) = 1.0157e-14 = 0.000109 a_0, ratio to g_N,inv = 0.714
  [FAIL] B1 E1 compares like with like.  The claim's central number 6.02e-15 must be the same physical quantity as the reconstruction it is compared to.  It is not: the baryonic side includes M31 at 0.77 Mpc and the whole Local Volume, the 2M++ side is masked to R > 3 Mpc/h and contains neither.  This check asserts the two volumes agree to 20%; it fails, and the direction of the failure is that E1's quoted g_B is a cancellation residual between an included near term and the far term   (g06's g_B = 6.024e-15 (far+near, partly cancelling) against the volume-matched g_B = 1.016e-14: a factor 1.69.  Matched, E1's ratio would be 0.714 rather than 0.424)
  NOTE, AGAINST MY OWN CASE: the volume-matched number moves E1's ratio TOWARD 1, so this front damages the
  precision of E1's quoted number without reversing its sign.  It is recorded because the claim quotes
  6.02e-15 as 'the direct baryonic sum at the Local Group' and that is not what was compared.
  directions: baryonic (l,b) = (181, +15); 2M++ (l,b) = (268, +40); CMB dipole apex for the Local Group is (l,b) ~ (276, +30) (Kogut et al. 1993)
  [FAIL] B2 the two fields point the same way.  E1 compares MAGNITUDES only.  Two vectors of similar length pointing 60 degrees apart are not 'the same field seen two ways'.  Asserts 30 degrees   (g06's g_B is 78 degrees from the 2M++ vector; the volume-matched baryonic vector is 6 degrees from it)

==============================================================================================================================
C.  THE PECULIAR-VELOCITY TIE-BREAK, DONE WITH LINEAR THEORY INSTEAD OF v ~ g t_0
==============================================================================================================================
  g06 breaks the tie with v ~ g t_0 and reports 'both routes in the right decade'.  Linear theory fixes the
  constant exactly: v = 2 f g / (3 H_0 Omega_m), f = Omega_m^0.55 (Peebles 1980; Strauss & Willick 1995).
      f = Omega_m^0.55 = 0.528, Omega_m = 0.3134, H_0 = 67.4 km/s/Mpc  ->  v = 5.145e+17 s x g   (g06 used t_0 = 4.350e+17 s, -15%)
    route                                                     g_dyn (m/s^2)  v_pred (km/s)    vs 620
    2M++ total-matter Newtonian field, used as the dynamics       1.161e-12            597      0.96
    baryons only, boosted by the kernel: nu(g_B/a0) g_B           7.539e-13            388      0.63
    ... same, on the volume-matched baryonic field                9.801e-13            504      0.81
  [FAIL] C1 the peculiar-velocity cross-check does not favour the reconstruction over the baryons.  g06 offers it as support for its reading ('both are in the right decade').  Done with the exact linear-theory constant rather than v ~ g t_0, this asserts the two routes miss the observed 620 km/s by comparable factors.  If it fails, the one piece of DATA g06 brings to E1 points the other way   (2M++ route 597 km/s, off by 4%; baryons-through-the-kernel 388 km/s, off by 37% (volume-matched 504 km/s, 19%).  Carrick+2015 fit beta* = 0.431 to this same dipole with this same field and reproduce it; the baryons-only route needs g_B a factor 2.6 larger to do so)
  Read plainly: the reconstruction reproduces the Local Group's measured motion to a few per cent -- that is
  what Carrick+2015 CALIBRATED it to do -- and the baryons-through-the-kernel route falls short by ~1.7x in
  velocity, i.e. ~3x in g_N.  That is inside g06's admitted completeness bound, so it is not a kill; but it
  is not support either, and g06 presents it as support.

