D.  HOW MUCH DOES E1 ACTUALLY CONSTRAIN?  The window is a factor 6.25 wide on g_B
==============================================================================================================================
  E1 passes for 0.4 < g_B/g_N,inv < 2.5, i.e. g_B anywhere in [5.687e-15, 3.555e-14] m/s^2 = [0.000061, 0.000380] a_0 -- a factor 6.25, or 0.80 dex.
  g06 states its baryonic sum is a LOWER bound: 2MRS is magnitude-limited, the zone of avoidance is
  unmasked, and no selection-function or 1/Vmax weighting is applied.  Three completeness scalings:
    assumed correction to g_B                      g_B (m/s^2)   E1 ratio  E1 verdict
    none (g06 as run)                                6.024e-15      0.424        PASS
    x2 (mild incompleteness)                         1.205e-14      0.847        PASS
    x3 (g06's own R4 bracket)                        1.807e-14      1.271        PASS
    x5                                               3.012e-14      2.119        PASS
    x10                                              6.024e-14      4.237        fail
    x0.5 (if 2MRS over-counted)                      3.012e-15      0.212        fail
  [FAIL] D1 E1 is a tight enough test to certify the baryonic sum at the precision the claim needs.  The claim rests on g_B being ~6e-5 a_0 rather than ~1e-2 a_0, but it is quoted as if E1 pinned the number.  This asserts that a threefold completeness correction -- the size g06 itself brackets in R4 -- would be DETECTED by E1   (g_B x3 gives an E1 ratio of 1.271, which is inside E1's [0.4, 2.5] window, so E1 cannot tell the two apart.  E1 admits g_B over 0.80 dex)
          2MRS shell       N  median K  faintest M_K  sum L_K (1e10)  |g| contribution
            5-20 Mpc     715      9.32        -17.81          1805.6         5.881e-15
           20-40 Mpc    1828      9.84        -19.85          7628.2         2.773e-15
           40-70 Mpc    4852     10.39        -21.45         33777.5         2.827e-15
          70-100 Mpc    7918     10.76        -22.61         74704.6         1.514e-15
         100-150 Mpc   12861     11.06        -23.37        185439.8         1.195e-15
  The faintest galaxy 2MRS still sees at 100-150 Mpc is roughly M_K ~ -24, i.e. several times L*.  The
  luminosity actually summed there is therefore a small fraction of the luminosity present, and the
  un-weighted sum used for g_B is an underestimate by an amount this script cannot pin down.  That is not a
  criticism of g06's honesty -- g06 says so -- it is the reason E1 cannot be load-bearing.

