E.  THE PREMISE: 'in this framework the actual matter is BARYONS' is retracted by this repository's own
    STANDING.md, and the retraction is exactly on the scales the external field comes from
==============================================================================================================================
      STANDING.md contains YES:  ""No dark matter" is forfeited"
      STANDING.md contains YES:  "MOND galaxies **plus** a
   no-particle CDM-like sector"
      STANDING.md contains YES:  "no-CDM MOND cosmologies fail the forest"
      STANDING.md contains YES:  "makes MOND irrelevant to linear growth"
      g06 asserts the premise verbatim: YES  ("In this framework the actual matter is BARYONS.")
  [FAIL] E-A the premise g06 argues from is the repository's live position.  g06's whole prescription argument is 'in QUMOND the external field is the Newtonian field of the actual matter, and in this framework the actual matter is BARYONS'.  The first clause is right.  This checks the second against STANDING.md, and it fails: STANDING section 5 item 5 records 'No dark matter is forfeited -- the framework HAS a dark sector, the AeST/ghost-condensate Q-mode -- MOND galaxies PLUS a no-particle CDM-like sector'   (STANDING.md carries the forfeit (True) and g06 carries the premise (True); they are contradictory and the claim inherits the contradiction)
  [FAIL] E-B and if the framework's CDM-like sector did NOT cluster on 10-100 Mpc scales, the contradiction would be harmless -- the external field would still be baryonic.  This checks the repository's own record on that.  It fails: STANDING records the sheet N-body result that no-CDM MOND cosmologies fall 1000-5000x short of the Lyman-alpha forest, and that with the framework's own Hubble floor MOND is a <= 6% correction to linear growth.  A CDM-like component that clusters, in a linear regime where MOND barely matters, is precisely what a 2M++ velocity-field reconstruction measures   (forest clause present: True; linear-growth clause present: True.  Both present means the framework's own committed cosmology sources the 10-100 Mpc Newtonian field with baryons PLUS the Q-mode, which is the total clustering matter the reconstruction returns)
  
  CONSEQUENCE, in g06's own currency.  g06's variation table already contains the answer under the label
  '2M++ field used raw as g_N (wrong, shown)': median boost 2.215 (+0.345 dex), inside the cluster band,
  against the primary 0.817.  That is g06's own R4b, which g06 marks FAIL and explains as a strawman.  On
  the repository's own standing it is not a strawman: it is the framework's own dark sector doing what
  STANDING says it does.  The intermediate case matters too -- a Q-mode that clusters on supercluster
  scales but is dilute inside a 0.2 Mpc group leaves the INTERNAL field baryonic while raising the EXTERNAL
  one, and that is exactly the branch R4b computes.

    external field sourced by baryons + Q-mode       e_N (a_0)   nu(e_N)  e_N/x_int, median group
    Q-mode contributes   0% of the total-matter field     0.00006    125.15                     0.03
    Q-mode contributes  10% of the total-matter field     0.00130     28.26                     0.69
    Q-mode contributes  25% of the total-matter field     0.00315     18.33                     1.67
    Q-mode contributes  50% of the total-matter field     0.00623     13.17                     3.30
    Q-mode contributes 100% of the total-matter field     0.01240      9.49                     6.56
  At any Q-mode share above ~10% of the total-matter field the external field exceeds the median group's own
  internal field and the external-field branch takes over.  The claim needs the share to be essentially ZERO.

