==============================================================================================================================
I.  TWO NAMED DEFECTS IN THE CLAIM'S HEADLINE NUMBER, AND ONE COMMITTED SIBLING THAT CONTRADICTS IT
==============================================================================================================================
  I.a  The exclusion rule for a group's OWN members is (name != host) AND (main_disturber != host).  The UNGC
       lists the SMC's main disturber as the LMC, not the Milky Way (Karachentsev, Makarov & Kaisina 2013),
       so the SMC survives the filter and is counted as an EXTERNAL perturber of the Milky Way -- at 0.06
       Mpc.  Its larger companion the LMC, whose main disturber IS the Milky Way, is correctly removed.  The
       bookkeeping therefore drops the bigger member of the Magellanic pair and keeps the smaller one.
       SMC: UNGC distance 0.060 Mpc, M_b = 1.02e+09 Msun, contribution 5.442e-15 m/s^2 = 0.90 x the whole quoted g_B of 6.024e-15
    Milky Way satellites removed by a distance cut   g_B (m/s^2)   e_N (a_0)   E1 ratio
    exclude UNGC galaxies within 0.0 Mpc of the MW     1.737e-14    0.000186      1.222
    exclude UNGC galaxies within 0.3 Mpc of the MW     7.215e-15    0.000077      0.507
    exclude UNGC galaxies within 0.5 Mpc of the MW     7.215e-15    0.000077      0.507
    exclude UNGC galaxies within 1.0 Mpc of the MW     9.742e-15    0.000104      0.685
  [FAIL] I1 the group's own members are excluded from its own external field.  The claim's headline number is the Milky Way group's external field; a Milky Way satellite 60 kpc away must not be in it.  This asserts the SMC contributes under 10% of g_B   (the SMC alone contributes 5.442e-15 m/s^2, 90% of the quoted g_B 6.024e-15; removing everything inside 0.3 Mpc of the Milky Way gives g_B = 7.215e-15, a factor 1.20)
  
  I.b  The repository already carries a committed, passing script that uses the OPPOSITE prescription for
       the SAME number.  h81_h82_mw_external_fields.py builds the 2M++ field with the identical code and
       calls it 'the NEWTONIAN large-scale field at the Local Group', tabulating e_N = 0.01240 canonical /
       0.01027 alt, and its check 81a is built on that reading.  g06 cites h81 for the reduction but not
       for the disagreement.  Two committed scripts, one quantity, a factor 193 apart.
       h81_h82_mw_external_fields.out tabulates LSS e_N = 0.01240 as a NEWTONIAN field: YES
  [FAIL] I2 the repository is internally consistent about which field enters nu's argument at the Local Group.  A prescription that 'must' hold cannot be contradicted by a committed sibling script that passes its own checks on the opposite reading   (h81_h82 (committed, passing) uses e_N = 0.01240 at the Local Group; g06 (this rung) uses e_N = 0.00006.  Factor 193.  One of the two is wrong and the repository does not say which)

