H.  MUTATION CONTROLS
==============================================================================================================================
  [PASS] M1 mutation -- shuffle the 2MRS baryonic masses across sky positions.  The dipole sum must change: if a scrambled catalogue gave the same g_B, the far field would be a property of the sky coverage rather than of where the mass is   (shuffled g_B = 4.564e-14 against the real 6.024e-15, +0.879 dex)
  [PASS] M2 mutation -- shuffle the 2M++ density cells.  The reconstruction must collapse toward zero; if it did not, the 1.16e-12 would be a normalisation artefact rather than a measurement of where the structure is   (shuffled g_2M++ = 1.342e-14 against the real 1.161e-12, a factor 0.0116)
  [PASS] M3 mutation -- stop excluding the Milky Way's own satellites from its external field.  The number must move, or the exclusion logic is not doing anything and the 'own group removed' claim is empty   (with no exclusion g_B = 1.737e-14 against 6.024e-15, +0.460 dex)
  [PASS] M4 mutation -- move the 2M++ inner mask from 3 to 1 Mpc/h.  If the reconstruction's value depended strongly on where its inner hole is cut, comparing it to a baryonic sum that has no such hole would be meaningless even in principle.  Asserts it moves by less than 30%   (mask R > 1 Mpc/h gives 1.177e-12 against 1.161e-12, a factor 1.014)

==============================================================================================================================
VERDICT SUMMARY
==============================================================================================================================
  What survives: the QUMOND half of the claim.  In QUMOND the external-field parameter is the Newtonian
  field of whatever sources the Newtonian potential -- that half is definitional and correct, and g06's
  arithmetic reproduces exactly (A1, A2).
  What does not survive: the identification of 'whatever sources the Newtonian potential' with BARYONS
  ALONE, on 10-100 Mpc scales, in a framework whose own STANDING.md forfeits 'no dark matter' and records a
  clustering CDM-like Q-mode plus a linear regime where MOND is a <= 6% correction (E-A, E-B).  On the
  repository's own standing the 2M++ reconstruction is closer to the right g_N,ext than the baryon sum is,
  and by g06's own R4b the rung's median boost then moves from 0.817 to 2.215 -- into the cluster band.
  What is weaker than advertised: E1 itself.  Its two sides are not the same volume (B1), its supporting
  velocity check runs against it once linear theory replaces v ~ g t_0 (C1), and its pass window admits g_B
  over 0.80 dex so it cannot certify the number the claim needs (D1).

